  "label": "Colloquial Vulgar Expression",
  "description": "The phrase 'my ass needed a break' is a vulgar, informal, self-deprecating expression used to convey physical exhaustion or relief from strain. It relies on common vernacular and mild profanity to communicate a relatable, humorous sentiment about needing rest after physical exertion. This expression is culturally understood in many English-speaking societies as a casual, non-harmful way to express fatigue.",
